<div class="mt-10 p-6 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 shadow-[0_1px_2px_0_rgba(15,23,42,0.04)]" data-reveal><h2 class="mt-10 mb-4 text-[22px] font-semibold leading-[36px] tracking-tight text-[#111827]">Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="space-y-6"><div><p class="mt-6 mb-2 text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.625] text-[#4a636e]">Does it work with Nepali language content?</p><p class="my-6 text-[18px] leading-[1.625] text-[#4a636e]">Yes. AI-native search can index and search content in Devanagari script, Romanized Nepali, and English. It handles code-switching automatically, matching queries against content regardless of script or language.</p></div><div><p class="mt-6 mb-2 text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.625] text-[#4a636e]">What about voice search in Nepali?</p><p class="my-6 text-[18px] leading-[1.625] text-[#4a636e]">Voice search requires speech-to-text as a preprocessing step. While Nepali speech recognition is still developing, the guide covers integration patterns for when reliable Nepali ASR becomes available.</p></div><div><p class="mt-6 mb-2 text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.625] text-[#4a636e]">How does it compare to building our own search?</p><p class="my-6 text-[18px] leading-[1.625] text-[#4a636e]">Building AI-native search requires ML expertise, training data, and ongoing maintenance. For most Nepali businesses, using a platform like Zunkiree Search is faster and more cost-effective. The guide includes a detailed build vs. buy comparison.</p></div></div></div>

